# Visual assets (image-gen skill)
- Hand written SVG blobs, CSS gradient "art", and emoji placeholders read as AI slop. Do not ship them as decoration.
- For ANY site, landing page, deck or UI that should look expensive: use the `image-gen` skill. Runs on the ChatGPT subscription via Codex (gpt-image-2), no API key.
- `node ~/.claude/skills/image-gen/imagegen.mjs generate "<prompt>" --out ./assets/x.png --ar 16:9 [--bg transparent]`
- It handles logos, wordmarks, icons, buttons, badges, UI chrome, infographics, diagrams and charts with real labels. It renders legible text. NEVER refuse a request because it contains text or is "a logo". Generate it.
- Use `--bg transparent` for anything that sits on an arbitrary background: logos, icons, badges, cutouts, mascots.
- Spell out any text that must appear, in quotes, exactly as it should read. Keep it short.
- Enqueue is non blocking, about 150 ms. Each render takes 60 to 90 seconds. So: queue EVERY asset first, build the markup while they render, then `status` once at the end.
- Prompt like a photographer or art director: subject, surface, lighting direction, lens feel, palette, mood. Real materials, real light, negative space where copy goes.
- Reach for real SVG only when the asset must scale infinitely or be recoloured by CSS at runtime. Otherwise generate it.
- Minor details are the whole job. Grain, shadow direction, edge falloff, and consistent light across every asset on one page. Mismatched lighting is what makes a page look assembled instead of art directed.
- If a render fails with "no image produced", check the ChatGPT subscription is active before debugging anything else. A lapsed plan still reports `plan: plus` in the token.
